{"kind":"artifact","text":"Documentation set with both reviewed P1s repaired, unmerged on branch task/docs at 1551a253. Both findings from ed57d24d were correct, and both were hidden by how I tested rather than by anything subtle in the text: I drove every command through an absolute path to the binary, so the missing PATH could not surface, and I cloned the audit copy directly from the source repository, whose refs/seq were already local, so the unpublished-sequence failure could not surface either. Install now puts bin/ on PATH and names the substitution for readers who would rather not, so the ordered steps resolve from the separate repository the next step moves them into. Publishing the sequence is now its own step: git neither pushes nor fetches refs/seq/* by default, attach arranges only the fetch side, and the exact failure a reader meets otherwise is quoted so the cause is recognisable. The same push sits beside attach in the reference. Re-tested by executing the page verbatim instead of driving the tools: PATH exported as written, bare command names, a workroom created in a separate repository, the loop carried to a satisfied commitment, and the audit taken from a clone of a bare remote that received the sequence only through the documented push. 29 links and anchors across 19 files resolve; make vet, make test, and make build pass. Not reviewed at this head and not merged.","body":{"commit":"1551a2533c64aafa41cfe645a0ded4886f4ebd13","path":"."}}